<<~ ahu #/entry>>
! Pair A: Ur and brutalist construction

The Operator steers the Ur trial away from excavation photogrammetry toward a
modern, smaller reconstruction, and holds nosycat's CC0 OpenSCAD/STL kit as
the complementary procedural witness. That steering names the experiment;
it does not grant a remote file a source digest.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/pattern-integrities>>
!! Source and hypothesis travel separately

* ''The source carries its own bytes.'' A third-party URL, visible download button,
  copyright notice or published dimensions do not attest to a local mesh;
  only ingested bytes carry a verified digest.
* ''The interpretive solid declares itself.'' The Ur terrace and stairs grow
  as authored CAD hypotheses informed by historical reports. Uncertain upper
  stages and the shrine retain explicit speculative status.
* ''The other language testifies.'' OpenSCAD and CadQuery MAY express related
  geometry independently. Similar silhouettes test adapters and projections,
  not agreement with the archaeological site.
* ''One body per CAD gate.'' STL and GLB contribute external surface testimony;
  they cannot certify physically connected solids or void circulation.
* ''The pair retains a bearing.'' A named location may carry conflicting measured
  extents and multiple seed geometries without forcing one into certainty.
* ''Slack preserves alternatives.'' Different valid architectures can survive,
  and the Operator can pet-name an interesting emergence or o-takiage a branch.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/afterward>>
!! Re-entry gates

Once actual History Builds and nosycat source bytes enter the evidence stack,
register orientation and units first, then compare fixed multi-view witnesses
under bounded OODA-HA epochs. Until that moment, synthetic previews can
validate the machina's mechanics but not the external reconstruction's fidelity.
<<~/ahu>>

